  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_building.header": "Building a Pika Power",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_building.text_1": "Start with the Pika Power Base. It is two blocks tall and makes its own rotation, so it needs no shafts, cogs or stress",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_building.text_2": "Nothing has to hold it up, but keep the block underneath clear. That face is the only one it gives energy back out of",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_building.text_3": "Ring the base with belts, two segments to a side, so the loop closes all the way round",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_building.text_4": "Every side of the ring is driven from the base, so the whole loop runs one way round and the Pokémon all face with it",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_building.text_5": "Cap the base with a Lightning Rod. The charge arcs up into its tip",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_pokemon.header": "Powering a Pika Power",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_pokemon.text_1": "Right click the base to open its Power Mice panel",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_pokemon.text_2": "Send up to eight Pikachu out of your PC and onto the belts.",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_pokemon.text_3": "Each one holds its own spot on the belt and runs in place.",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_pokemon.text_4": "Their charge arcs into the rod. Every Pikachu adds power in step with its level, so a full ring of high levels produce the most",
  "allthemons.ponder.pika_power_pokemon.text_5": "The base stores the charge as FE. Run a cable from its bottom face to pull the charge back out",
